cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "CNS5-Audit: Integrated WHO CNS5 Classification, Multi-Standard RANO Calculators, and Neuro-AI Data-Leakage Auditing Suite"
message: "If you use CNS5-Audit in your clinical research, peer review, methodological audit, or educational materials, please cite this software using the metadata below."
type: software
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-11-20"
license: MIT
authors:
  - name: "CNS5-Audit Contributors"
abstract: >-
  CNS5-Audit is an open-source, zero-build, 100% browser-local web suite that
  unifies three core neuro-oncology research and peer-review workflows:
  (1) a deterministic WHO CNS5 (2021) integrated molecular-histological tumor
  classifier covering all major CNS tumor families with mandatory Arabic-numeral
  grading, molecular upgrade tracking, and NOS/NEC guidance;
  (2) multi-standard clinical response and resection calculators implementing
  RANO 2.0, RANO-BM, and RANO-Resect with strict monotonicity, baseline, and
  volumetric boundary guards; and
  (3) a 36-item Neuro-AI data-leakage and reporting auditor cross-mapped to
  CLAIM 2024 and TRIPOD+AI with an automated Critical Blocker score cap and
  publication-ready Markdown, LaTeX, SVG badge, and JSON exporters.
  All computation executes locally in the browser with zero external uploads.
  For research and educational use only; not a certified medical device.
keywords:
  - WHO CNS5
  - neuro-oncology
  - glioma
  - RANO 2.0
  - RANO-BM
  - RANO-Resect
  - CLAIM 2024
  - TRIPOD+AI
  - data leakage
  - radiomics
  - neuro-AI
  - clinical research software
  - open science
  - peer review
